Hi {{adjuster_name}},

I'm requesting a reinspection on the claim for {{client_name}} ({{claim_number}}). During review, we identified the following that we don't believe was captured in the original inspection:

- {{disputed_item_1}}
- {{disputed_item_2}}

I've attached supporting photos/documentation. Could we get this scheduled? Happy to work around your availability.

Thanks,
{{your_name}}

Hi {{recipient_name}},

To move forward on the claim for {{claim_number}}, I need the following:

- {{item_needed_1}}
- {{item_needed_2}}

This will help us {{why_it_matters}}. Let me know if you have any questions, or if there's anything I can do to help get this together.

Thanks,
{{your_name}}

Hi {{adjuster_name}},

Re: {{client_name}} — Claim {{claim_number}} — Date of loss {{date_of_loss}}

We're requesting a reinspection of the above loss. This letter, with the attached line-item comparison, also serves as written, itemized documentation of a specific dispute as to the amount of the loss under the Appraisal condition of the policy. Each disputed item is listed separately below:

1. {{disputed_item_1}} — State Farm: {{sf_amount_1}} | Ours: {{our_amount_1}} | Basis: {{reason_1}}
2. {{disputed_item_2}} — State Farm: {{sf_amount_2}} | Ours: {{our_amount_2}} | Basis: {{reason_2}}
3. {{disputed_item_3}} — State Farm: {{sf_amount_3}} | Ours: {{our_amount_3}} | Basis: {{reason_3}}

Total amount in dispute: {{total_difference}} (State Farm estimate {{sf_total}} vs. our estimate {{our_total}}).

Attached: our estimate, the line-item comparison, and supporting photos/documentation.

Please confirm receipt of this letter and its attachments by reply. If reinspection is declined, or the dispute isn't resolved, the insured reserves the right to demand appraisal once 10 days have passed from your receipt of this notice.

Thanks,
{{your_name}}
